From: Nagarajan <nagarajan.02s5@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 07:18:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add HPA, PDB tuning and Prometheus/Grafana monitoring

- k8s: add HPA (testing 1-2, prod 2-6) on the frontend container CPU; remove
  hardcoded Deployment replicas so the HPA owns scaling; prod PDB now uses
  maxUnavailable: 1; prod pods spread across zones
- k8s: add nginx-prometheus-exporter sidecar and a metrics Service port;
  expose stub_status on 127.0.0.1:8080 in nginx.conf
- monitoring: kube-prometheus-stack values tuned for EKS, gp3 storage class,
  ServiceMonitor, PrometheusRule alerts, Grafana dashboard
- ci: add monitoring.yml workflow (validate, then deploy behind the production

  environment approval)
- docs: monitoring/README.md and a README section

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
